       <section anchor="obsolete-protocols" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-6.10">
         <name slugifiedName="name-obsolete-protocols">Obsolete Protocols</name>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-6.10-1">Some of the protocols listed in this memo are described in RFCs that are
+obsoleted by newer RFCs.  &quot;Obsolete&quot; or &quot;obsoleted&quot; is not an official
+state or status of protocols.  This subsection is for information only.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-6.10-2">While it may seem to be obviously wrong to have an obsoleted RFC in the
+list of standards, there may be cases when an older standard is in the
+process of being replaced.  This process may take a year or two.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-6.10-3">Many obsoleted protocols are of little interest and are dropped from
+this memo altogether.  Some obsoleted protocols have received enough
+recognition that it seems appropriate to list them under their current
+status and with the following reference to their current replacement.</t>
+        <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-6.10-4"><![CDATA[
